GNU Make and executable dependency workflows (@rc-make: 0, is #reference, #part-of @rc-sources) { r_6Y907BH3SMATGCHV3C7ZC2CVMF
Free Software Foundation and GNU Make contributors. GNU Make manual. [Official manual](https://www.gnu.org/software/make/manual/) · [Full HTML manual](https://www.gnu.org/software/make/manual/make.html). For a second practical reading use the Make chapter of Research Software Engineering with Python and the Make chapter of The Turing Way.

Read the introduction, rules, prerequisites, recipes, variables, phony targets, errors, and parallel-execution material. Reconstruct a small dependency graph and test what happens when an input changes, an output is absent, a recipe fails, or a configuration value is not declared as a prerequisite. More advanced patterns are useful only after these basic semantics are understood.

The GNU manual has its own free-documentation terms; preserve its notices before adaptation. The official manual endpoints timed out during automated checking on 29 October 2026. The verified author-book and Turing Way chapters provide accessible practical readings and identify the same tool; record the installed version and consult its supplied manual as well. No manual copy is bundled.

**Return:** [Reproducible-computation sources — books, research, and primary manuals](../Sources.lingua#r_7RY36NATQ0VQE5JMJAMF6KXK3K).
